      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitoregon.com/cities/dundee-oregon/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dundee was named after Dundee, Scotland, the birthplace of William Reid, a Scottish immigrant who settled in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundee%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "William Reid arrived in Oregon in 1874 to establish the Oregonian Railway and expand rail lines through the Willamette Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dundee%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
